00:35:07.829 --> 00:35:12.550
but to make it concrete
and progress the discussion

00:35:13.514 --> 00:35:18.067
and then, Ruzica, I think
we met with this morning

00:35:18.067 --> 00:35:18.900
who's great.

00:35:18.900 --> 00:35:20.423
Yeah, we sort of couldn't stop.

00:35:21.300 --> 00:35:23.211
- She's fabulous,
- She's great,

00:35:23.211 --> 00:35:25.920
but we really sort of mind melded

00:35:25.920 --> 00:35:28.320
on this idea of abstraction layers.

00:35:28.320 --> 00:35:30.780
And so I spend a lot of my time at Google

00:35:30.780 --> 00:35:33.000
trying to convince these
engineers that it's, you know,

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:34.560
in the early days of Google,

