mathematical questions

00:37:27.150 --> 00:37:29.580
become part of how the algorithms work.

00:37:29.580 --> 00:37:31.410
I mean in terms of how you
do search through language

00:37:31.410 --> 00:37:32.640
and how you represent language.

00:37:32.640 --> 00:37:33.473
- Totally.

00:37:34.392 --> 00:37:35.600
- All of these things
you're talking about.

00:37:36.591 --> 00:37:37.597
- I mean one just quick example of that

00:37:38.973 --> 00:37:40.428
that sort of, I mean, makes
sense but surprised me

00:37:40.428 --> 00:37:44.580
was that if you train
a model on just text,

00:37:44.580 --> 00:37:45.573
sort of one mode,

00:37:46.800 --> 00:37:48.750
and you train even with a smaller amount

00:37:48.750 --> 00:37:52.230
of the image and text,

00:37:52.230 --> 00:37:56.440
that second model is better at text only

00:37:57.450 --> 00:38:00.780
because to your point, our
ideas and what we understand

00:38:00.780 --> 00:38:04.563
are not perfectly abstracted to language.

00:38:04.563 --> 00:38:05.396
- [Jeffrey] Right.

00:38:05.396 --> 00:38:07.187
- And in fact it learns something

00:38:07.187 --> 00:38:09.765
that we don't express directly.

00:38:09.765 --> 00:38:11.730
It's loss-y right.

00:38:11.730 --> 00:38:15.120
Language to ideas loses information.

00:38:15.120 --> 00:38:16.530
- Right.

